1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:08,500
I’m Wariddon Rattanamalee. I build banking APIs at SCB and tools for the staff who review orders at InblackM.

2
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:19,180
I started in insurance in 2018. Since then I’ve worked on telecom services, access management and banking systems. Let me show you a few examples.

3
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:29,821
At Thai Insurance, I built an API that sent policy data to the insurance regulator in real time. I handled the certificates and encryption for that connection.

4
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:36,532
I also worked on TMB Tablet and the systems staff used for agents, partners and account statements.

5
00:00:37,367 --> 00:00:43,823
At CAT Telecom, I built Java and Spring Boot features and helped test them against what the business needed.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,157
At TISCO, I built Python services and Angular screens for user access. I also worked on digital signatures and helped test performance with LoadRunner.

7
00:00:53,433 --> 00:01:01,419
At SCB, my role is Software engineering, Full Stack Developer. I build banking APIs in Java and Spring Boot.

8
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:09,055
During the SCB Connect migration, I helped update the gateway and trace issues the team found during user acceptance testing.

9
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:19,365
One Redis service could outlive its login token. I changed how it renews the token and switches connection pools, so it reconnects with fresh credentials.

10
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:28,653
For monthly AML reports, I made sure the team gets a different email when there’s no data and when delivery fails. Those need different follow-up.

11
00:01:28,933 --> 00:01:37,622
I also work part-time at InblackM as a Senior Tech Development Consultant. I build order review and pricing screens in React and Next.js.

12
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:44,452
When staff hand over an order, I check who owns it and whether it’s still open. The queue and order record change together.

13
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:54,016
I use Claude and Codex to trace requests across services or follow an order from the staff screen to the worker that handles it.

14
00:01:56,200 --> 00:02:05,752
I read the changes and run the tests myself. For our read-only admin assistant, I also check the references and keep the original search results available.

15
00:02:06,533 --> 00:02:14,821
I studied computer science at Burapha University and later completed an MBA in finance and banking at Ramkhamhaeng University.

16
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:19,804
Thanks for listening. You can find the slides and my resume on my portfolio.
